{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0002": "$y \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{D})$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\mapsto \\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(x), y)$", "MATH_0004": "$u$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-adjoint-exists}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:edd900fbcc9fc5f71294c4f43870a26c2238dc7f9f0a7923b526c351d8ea0e09", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:89930a490bfcfc9db946fbc6eb1c81632016c9124b3dcc59c0e56daa88e51412", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a functor between categories.\nIf for each <MATH_0002> the functor\n<MATH_0003> is representable, then\n<MATH_0004> has a right adjoint.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4cf8b70bdc6928fc743290c71896bb2874484a794201c7c1836b4a7bc914cd97", "unit_id": "tag:0A8B:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$y$", "MATH_0002": "$v(y)$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(-, v(y)) \\to \\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(-), y)$", "MATH_0004": "$g : y \\to y'$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(-, v(y)) \\to \\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(-), y) \\to\n\\Mor_\\mathcal{D}(u(-), y') \\to \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(-, v(y'))\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$v(g) : v(y) \\to v(y')$", "MATH_0007": "$v$", "MATH_0008": "$u$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-yoneda}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4e56e6fadb05972f42db9ad2ce8e565b022da967dd54360b88a90426615f9976", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:76359c10df7945c63b70218916a5825f5e396a8e54f4ef7008cb051a71b2981d", "source_text": "For each <MATH_0001> choose an object <MATH_0002> and an isomorphism\n<MATH_0003>\nof functors. By Yoneda's lemma (Lemma <REF_0001>)\nfor any morphism <MATH_0004> the transformation of functors\n<MATH_0005>\ncorresponds to a unique morphism <MATH_0006>.\nWe omit the verification that <MATH_0007> is a functor and that\nit is right adjoint to <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59410e9f4551dd5a2ba148b6e2052292fc50f6fb189418cf6faeb237a72e2c16", "unit_id": "tag:0A8B:proof"}
